              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मना करना — manā karnā — \"to forbid; to say no\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अगर डाक्टर मना करेगा तो मैं मिठाई नहीं खाऊँगा। agar ḍākṭar manā karegā to maiṁ miṭhāī nahīṃ khāūṅgā. If the doctor forbids it, I won't eat sweets."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with ने (he or she …): उसने मना किया, usne manā kiyā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मना करना (manā karnā) joins मना to करना, \"to do\". मना is usually traced to Arabic manʿ, \"prevention, holding back\", which reached Hindi through Persian."
            }
          ]
        },
